<.shell current={:filter_a_list}>
  <h1>Filter a list</h1>
  <p class="lead">The activity list: tiles, filters, a summary line, the table, and pages.</p>

  <div class="example">
    <.report_page
      id="sample-list"
      view={sample_activity_view()}
      records={%{}}
      team={sample_team()}
      now={nil}
      path_fn={fn _ -> "#" end}
      form={Web.Components.ReportPage.controls_form(sample_activity_view())}
      marker={&if(&1 == "all", do: nil, else: &1)}
    >
      <:table>
        <div class="table-actions">
          <.button type="button">Add to group</.button>
          <.button type="button">Remove from group</.button>
        </div>
        <.activity_table
          id="sample-activities"
          rows={activities()}
          sort="date-"
          path_fn={fn _ -> "#" end}
          team={sample_team()}
        />
      </:table>
    </.report_page>
  </div>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      The <a href={page_path(:stat_switch)}>stat switch</a> splits the list into counts.
    </li>
    <li>
      The <a href={page_path(:filter_bar)}>filter bar</a>
      sits above the table: a search box and a menu per filter. A menu that filters something turns blue.
    </li>
    <li>The line under it has the count and Clear filters, and which rows the page shows.</li>
    <li>
      Actions on ticked rows, such as Add to group, go in a <code>.table-actions</code>
      row under it, sized like the bar: 36px, small text, 44px on a touch screen.
    </li>
    <li>The column headers sort the table.</li>
    <li><a href={page_path(:pagination)}>Pagination</a> goes under the table, 50 rows a page.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="spec">
    In the app: <code>&lt;.report_page&gt;</code>, which draws the tiles, the bar, and the pages from the list's report (<code>App.Report.Lists</code>). The page passes its own table, here
    <code>&lt;.activity_table&gt;</code>
    with made-up activities.
  </p>
</.shell>
